#
# The upstream provenance of the vendored benchmark harness.
#
# These three files are copied byte-for-byte from
# hyperpolymath/proven-tests-and-benches, at the revision below. They are
# vendored rather than fetched at run time so the gate runs offline and on a
# contributor's machine; `scripts/proven-bench/verify-upstream.sh` fetches
# the same revision from upstream and compares the digests, so a vendored
# copy that drifts is caught rather than trusted.
#
# The estate's testing taxonomy says to draw from proven-tests-and-benches
# FIRST, ahead of writing a new test or benchmark: copying a test is how a
# shared expectation stays shared, and writing a fresh one per repository is
# how sixteen subtly different definitions of "the same" test appear.
#
# Format: shell assignments, sourced by verify-upstream.sh.
